The infobox used at the top of '''<code>/chorus</code> subpages''' of famous utattemita songs. It renders a navigation bar linking back to the parent song's cover list and across to the chorus list, plus a note pointing readers to the definition of a chorus. Pages using it are filed under [[:Category:Famous Utattemita Songs/chorus]].

==Syntax==
{{T|Chorus|v1=root =}}

==Usage==
This template is shown as code only — a live call would add this documentation page to [[:Category:Famous Utattemita Songs/chorus]].
<pre>
{{Chorus}}
</pre>
Place it at the top of a page named <code>Song Name/chorus</code>. The navigation links are built from the base page name automatically, so no parameters are needed in the normal case.

If the parent page does not exist under the expected name, point the "Song covers" link somewhere else with <code>root</code>:
<pre>
{{Chorus|root=Actual Song Page}}
</pre>

